Vikram and Betal: The Three Questions

King Vikram was carrying Betal through the forest once again.

Betal began his story.

“Once there was a king who loved asking questions,” said Betal. “He asked everyone three questions.”

The questions were:
“When is the right time to act?”
“Who is the most important person?”
“What is the most important thing to do?”

No one in the court could answer correctly.

One day, a wise man came to the king.

The king asked him the same questions.

The wise man replied, “The right time is now. The most important person is the one you are with. The most important thing is to do good.”

The king was very pleased with his answers.

Betal then asked, “Vikram, why were these answers correct?”

Vikram replied, “Because they teach us to live in the present and do good to others.”

As soon as Vikram spoke, Betal flew back to the tree.

💖 Moral:

Always do good in the present moment.
